column29:
Prediction question: participants were asked whether the butterfly's DNA would exhibit a mutation and answer either "YES, the mutation will occur" or "NO, the mutation will not occur."; causal probe question: “To what extent does radiation cause mutations?”;
frequentist counterfactual probe question: "How many out of 100 butterflies, none of which would show a mutation in the test if unradiated, do you estimate would show a mutation if radiated?”; single-event counterfactual question: “How likely would a butterfly, which would not show a mutation in the test if unradiated, be to show a mutation in the test if radiated?”
After the judgment scale, the participants were required to indicate how confident they were in the judgment

